#reason .gitattributes Keeps the Windows batch script CRLF on checkout, since cmd label lookup misbehaves with LF.
#reason src/cli/lantern.cmd Gives Windows a lantern command that opens a folder or a --compare review from a terminal.
#reason src/main/cli-user-install.ts Installs the command per user on Linux and Windows through an injectable port so it is testable.
#reason src/main/cli-user-port.ts Provides the real file-system and PowerShell user-PATH access, never rewriting the PATH on a failed read.
#reason test/cli-user-install.test.ts Proves the Linux link and PATH hint, the Windows shim and PATH-once rule, and a safe PATH read.
#reason docs/installation.md Tells Linux and Windows users how the command is installed, not only macOS users.
#reason src/cli/lantern Lets the same command start the packaged Linux executable instead of only calling macOS open.
#reason src/main/cli.ts Lets the script path follow the platform and carries the optional note on the status.
#reason src/main/main.ts Routes the command channels to the per-user installer off macOS and keeps macOS as it was.
#reason src/renderer/features/cli-panel.ts Shows the PATH hint and new-terminal note and drops the macOS-only wording.
#reason test/cli-panel.test.ts Covers the Linux and Windows notes and guides in the panel.
#reason test/cli-script.test.ts Proves the script starts the packaged Linux executable with the folder as --project.
#reason test/settings-dialog.test.ts Follows the panel's new wording for an unsupported or development run.
#story A Linux user installs the lantern command
#step actor Linux user
#step action clicks Install in Command line settings
#file src/renderer/features/cli-panel.ts
#file src/main/main.ts
#step subject their own bin folder
#file src/main/cli-user-install.ts
#below interaction can open Lantern from any terminal
#file src/cli/lantern
#file test/cli-script.test.ts
#below consequence no lantern command on Linux => lantern works, with a hint when PATH lacks the folder
#file test/cli-user-install.test.ts
#story A Windows user installs the lantern command
#step actor Windows user
#step action clicks Install in Command line settings
#file src/renderer/features/cli-panel.ts
#step subject their user command folder and PATH
#file src/main/cli-user-install.ts
#file src/main/cli-user-port.ts
#below interaction can open Lantern from a new terminal
#file src/cli/lantern.cmd
#below consequence no lantern command on Windows => lantern works without admin rights
#file test/cli-user-install.test.ts
